  concept: "Authored objective: Establish the 45 RPM reference.\nAuthored requirement:
    Recorded from the electrical graph, valid calibrated feedback and the level\u2019s
    verified run history. voltage \u2265 4.8 V. voltage \u2264 5.2 V.\nGeneral teaching
    principle: Motor behavior depends on drive conditions, load, feedback and protective
    limits; test the observed state at each authored checkpoint.\nOnly fresh, authoritative
    game evidence can establish that this objective is complete."
  analogy: A controlled wheel under varying load shows why a command does not always
    equal actual speed.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: A drive command alone does not establish speed, torque or safe stopping.
  baseline: "Before working on \u2018Establish the 45 RPM reference\u2019, which
    component, reference or condition mentioned in the authored requirement should
    you inspect first? Explain your reasoning."
  prediction: "For \u2018Establish the 45 RPM reference\u2019, what result or observation
    would you expect if the required setup is correct? Distinguish a predicted result
    from a measured result."
  practice: "In Level 54, perform the objective \u2018Establish the 45 RPM reference\u2019
    in the actual game laboratory. Compare fresh evidence against: Recorded from
    the electrical graph, valid calibrated feedback and the level\u2019s verified
    run history. voltage \u2265 4.8 V. voltage \u2264 5.2 V.\nThe mission evaluator
    decides completion; this tutorial does not grade your answer."
